Sella-derived components
========================

Parts of this repository are derived from Sella 2.5.0:
https://github.com/zadorlab/sella

Sella copyright notice:

  Copyright 2019 National Technology & Engineering Solutions of Sandia,
  LLC (NTESS). Under the terms of Contract DE-NA0003525 with NTESS, the
  U.S. Government retains certain rights in this software.

Sella is distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 3.0.
The derived code was modified in 2026 for force-call-constrained molecular
geometry optimization. The modifications include adapting the optimizer
interface, making selected implementations self-contained, enforcing exact
force-call accounting, handling refused potential evaluations, and changing
optimization mechanisms developed during the reported autoresearch runs.

Derived or adapted files include:

  minimizers/autosella_f.py
  minimizers/autosella_g.py
  minimizers/autosella_a.py
  minimizers/sella_baseline.py

The corresponding source is included in this repository. The experiment
branches preserve the development history of the selected modifications.


Third-party software and data
=============================

AutoSella uses third-party scientific packages including ASE, JAX, NumPy,
OpenFF Toolkit, OpenMM, RDKit, SciPy, Sella, xTB, and xyz2mol. Those packages
are not redistributed under the AutoSella license merely because they appear
in an environment specification; their own licenses apply.

Molecular data derived from SPICE, RowanSci, PubChem, and other upstream sources
retain their respective upstream licenses, terms, and citation requirements.
The LGPL license covering AutoSella software does not relicense those data.
